    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `presigned_download.py` that generates a time-limited signed download URL for a stored object, I need to choose a concrete external provider. Amazon S3 is a widely used service for managed object storage, and it provides a method to generate presigned URLs. I will use the Boto3 library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, to interact with S3. The code will import Boto3 and use it to create a presigned URL for a specified S3 object. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789850087389,
          "start": 1789850085123
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bb60e703001sIu1IXGm1SdIlC",
